## Protected Files

- **File access override:** read any path the user provides, regardless of `.gitignore`.
- **Framework source marker:** `agent.os.framework.md` at a repo root marks that repo as the Agent OS framework source. It exists only in the framework source repo — if you see it, repo-mode rules for the framework source apply. Never modify, rename, or delete it; never copy it into a consumer project.
- **Do NOT modify unless explicitly asked in the same message:** paths in `.work/PROTECTED_SURFACES.json` (compose/Dockerfiles, app config, the secrets-manager API contract, edge nginx, the wordlist that feeds the integrity digest). Consumer examples: `password/package.json`, `docker-compose.*.yml`, `Dockerfile.password.*`, `password/next.config.ts`, `password/eslint.config.mjs`, `password/postcss.config.mjs`, `.env*`.
- **If a protected file needs a change:** stop, explain why, ask permission; edit only after yes in that message (Core Principle 8).

---

## Data Privacy & Security

- **Sensitive data:** keep production/customer data local without approval; use the repo sanitizer (e.g. `.obfuscation/sanitize_data.py`) before loading exports/XML; prefer sanitized copies over raw.
- **No PII in logs:** never log full objects with PII (emails, phones, gov IDs, amounts) — log internal IDs/status only; sanitize errors.
- **Debug scripts:** no embedded sensitive data; use `.env` or runtime values; ask before re-running when a var is missing.
- **Secret scrubbing:** before reading/emitting text, ensure no keys/tokens/passwords appear (`[REDACTED]`); never display credentials or raw `.env`.
- **Test data:** synthetic/mock only; never hardcode real emails/IDs; no unsanitized prod dumps in tests.
- **File hygiene:** write `.xls/.xlsx/.csv/.xml/.json` exports to `tmp/`, not the source tree. Agent-created files under `tmp/` may be removed after use (sole exception to §Workflow Deletion).

---

## Database & Schema Rules

This project has **no relational database** — no tables, no SQL, no migrations. Runtime state is one encrypted JSON store (`store.json` + `master.key`) on the `secrets_data` named volume, served by `secrets-manager/`.

- **Persisted-state changes** (new secret kind, new store field, store-format change) need a design note in `.work/features/` and — when the wire contract changes — an update to `secrets-manager/openapi.yaml` plus an ADR in `.work/decisions/`. The store format version lives in `secrets-manager/lib/store.mjs`.
- **Destructive data ops (hard stop):** NEVER `DROP`/`TRUNCATE`/wipe a database, schema, or volume (`down -v`, recreate-empty, flush-all) unless the human authorizes that exact operation in the same message (Core Principle 8). This includes the `secrets_data` volume and the `restore`/`cleanup` verbs of `./bin/start.sh`.
- **Backfills: STRICTLY PROHIBITED** by agents against shared/dev stores — describe the operation for manual execution.
- `@db-migration` does not apply until a SQL database is introduced.

---

## Docker / Dev Environment

- When the project uses Compose, **never** run bare `npm/yarn/next/python/pytest/pip install` or type-checkers on the host — run all app test/lint/type/build commands inside the documented compose service. Installing service deps on the host bloats and dirties it; containers isolate the toolchain.

| Action | Where |
|--------|-------|
| Install deps for a service | Inside that service's compose container |
| Tests, lint, type-check, builds | `docker compose exec <service> …` |
| Rare host command | Only if `DOCS_TECH_STACK.md` documents it, or the user approves in-message |

```bash
# tests/lint/type — inside the dev app container (compose needs the env file)
docker compose --env-file .env.dev -f docker-compose.dev.yml exec app bash -c "cd /code/password && npm run typecheck && npm run lint"
# stack-level checks (host; they drive Docker themselves)
./bin/check-env-parity.sh
./bin/verify-secrets-manager.sh --env dev
```

Container identity comes from the env file (`COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`, ports, `APP_ENV`); prefer `./bin/start.sh` for isolated compose. Skills (`code-implementation`, `code-verify`) must use these commands, not hardcoded names from another project. Place one-off host scripts under `bin/`.

---

## Workflow Rules

- **Planning:** plans live under `.work/plans/`. Wait for approval before large code changes when a plan-only was requested; confirm before editing when scope is unclear.
- **Deletion:** NEVER delete files without explicit permission in the same message (Core Principle 8). Sole exception: agent-created `tmp/` cleanup (§Data Privacy).
- **Task refs** (e.g. `PROJ-456`, `PROJ-T-23`) link commits to work items:
  1. User-provided ref (request/HANDOFF/branch) → prepend `REF: ` to every commit subject.
  2. No ref but work belongs to a task → ask once before committing; never guess/invent.
  3. No ref (exploratory/docs/chore) → conventional `type:` is fine.
- **Git:**
  - NEVER `git commit`/`push` unless the user requests it in the same message (Core Principle 8).
  - **Human commit lane:** the operator may commit/push manually at any time — Core Principle 8 constrains the **agent**, not the operator. Plain `@session-control close` with a dirty tree is a valid pass: hand over the draft message (with task ref) + suggested `git add` scope; keep `.work/active-ref` so manual commits stay ref-linked; never stage operator WIP unless the invocation includes `commit`. No-attribution hooks stay hard-enforced (`prepare-commit-msg` strips, `commit-msg` rejects `Co-authored-by:`).
  - `@session-control close commit` / `commit` (and `push` variants): you MUST run shell `git add` + `git commit` per `.ai/skills/session-control/skill.md` (C4b / Commit protocol) — this is a consumer repo, so stage all safe changes under `.work/` **plus** root-level `PROCESS_ROUTER.md`, `DOCS_TECH_STACK.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` **if present** (default scope; includes new untracked files/dirs; secrets/`tmp/`/protected files excluded), then `git push` if requested. Show `git log -1 --oneline` + `git status -sb`; no "committed" claim without a SHA. `commit` variants skip HANDOFF/NEXT (session stays open).
  - `prepare-commit-msg` hook auto-prepends the ref when the branch contains one and strips `Co-authored-by:` trailers. Don't bypass hooks unless the user requests `--no-verify`.
  - Never modify history (rebase, force-push) without explicit request in the same message.
- **No attribution:** never add "Generated by", "Created by", dates, or agent signatures.
- **No `Co-authored-by:` (mandatory):** never add co-author trailers (Cursor/Copilot/any agent) or `--trailer`. Enforced by hooks (`prepare-commit-msg` strips, `commit-msg` rejects). Install once: `bash /mnt/work/Projects/pilo.ai.logicbison/scripts/install-git-hooks.sh` (auto via bootstrap/deploy).

---

## Verification & Communication

- **Before "complete":** run applicable tests + lint/type; confirm no regression; report actual output, not assumed.
- **On failure:** report exact error, diagnose root cause, fix, re-run.
- **Scope:** declare scope first (§ Change safety); `touch-scope-verify` + `blast-radius-check` enforce it.
- **Communication:** be concise; surface blockers early; label uncertainty; distinguish confirmed facts / inferences / proposals.
- **Output economy:** see **Core Principle 9** (≤150-word chat budget + escalation gate). Minimal direct prose: no preambles, intros, request restatements, reasoning narration, or closing summaries.
- **Operator handoff (mandatory):** every response that ends a turn closes per `.ai/skills/SKILL_DEPENDENCIES.md` § Operator handoff contract — terse output; approvals under `**Needs your approval:**` citing `path:L<n>`; questions numbered under `**Needs your answer:**`; exactly one `**Next step:**` command; one line (Form A) when no input is needed; abstract plan/SPEC ids (`M4-T2`, `FR-7`, `U-12`) never bare — plain-language gloss + `path:L<n>` locator (contract rule 7). Decisions and questions never mixed; empty sections omitted.

---

## OpenSpec (optional)

If used: proposals first for new/significant changes; implement exactly as approved; lifecycle commands under `.ai/commands/openspec/`. If unused, delete this section.

## External docs

Use Context7 MCP (`@upstash/context7-mcp`) for version-specific library docs when configured; else web-search to verify current APIs before writing integration code.

---

## Commit Message Format

- Plain text; no surrounding quotes or wrapping parentheses.
- Subject (≤72 chars, imperative): `REF-123: subject` when a ref is known (HANDOFF, GitHub task registry, branch, or last commit), else `type: description`.
- Optional body after a blank line (~72 col): explain **why**, not the file list.
- Types (no ref): `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `style`, `test`.
- **Readable by all audiences:** subject understandable by non-technical stakeholders; keep jargon/codenames in the body.
- When `github_task_registry_enabled`, the AI may query `GET /v1/projects/{id}/github/task-registry` for the ref (optional; fall back to HANDOFF/branch/last-commit). Ref prefixes are auto-linked inbound on GitHub sync via `commit_subject_refs` (idempotent) — always prefer `REF: subject` when a ref is known.
- Correct: `PROJ-456: Add login form with email validation` · `fix: handle empty payload on webhook retry`. Wrong: `"fix(webhook): empty payload"`.

---

## Documentation layout (`.ai/` vs `.work/`)

- **`.ai/`:** framework-only — skills, concepts, workflow guides, `START_HERE.md`, `PROCESS_ROUTER.md`, `templates/`, plus framework-wide contract/schema docs (e.g. `MASTER_PLAN_STANDARD.md`). **Never created by `@deploy-basic`** (thin-client). Fat-client only via `@deploy-files` / `@project-bootstrap init` when you explicitly vend a local copy. Pointer READMEs only under `.ai/plans/`, `.ai/features/`.
- **`.work/`:** **all project-specific memory and customization** — plans, SPECs, ADRs, prompts, `HANDOFF.md`, `PROTECTED_SURFACES.json`, binding **`.work/standards/`**, and **`.work/docs/`** (including vendor **`.work/docs/integration/`** cache). Generated filenames use the `YYYYMMDD-` prefix (except `NEXT.md`, `HANDOFF.md`). Always local in **both** fat- and thin-client modes — never resolved from `$AGENT_OS_SOURCE`.

| Path | Layer |
|------|-------|
| `.work/plans/` | Plans, registries, `NEXT.md` |
| `.work/features/` | Feature SPECs |
| `.work/decisions/` | ADRs |
| `.work/prompts/` | Questionnaires; user scratch |
